course: dictionary
lesson: 8696
title: Selfless: putting others first
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A selfless person thinks about other people's needs and happiness before their own. The word is made of self, meaning you, and less, meaning without, so selfless means without thinking of yourself first. The context shows this: «In every gurdwara there is a langar, a free kitchen where anyone may sit on the floor and eat together, rich and poor side by side; this is seva, selfless service.» Feeding everyone for free, rich and poor alike, shows that the people serving put others first.
explain: The second sentence gives another clue: «Seva means selfless service to others, and it is central in Sikhism.» The word service tells you the meaning is about helping others. Use the swap check: put «helping others without wanting anything back» into the sentence in place of selfless. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Selfless is an adjective, so it describes a person or an act. You can say a selfless person, a selfless act, selfless love or selfless service. Its comparative forms are more selfless and most selfless.
fact: Selfless means thinking about other people's needs and happiness more than your own.
fact: A selfless act is something done to help others without wanting anything back.
fact: «Selfless» is an adjective: you can say «a selfless act» or «selfless love».
fact: «Seva» means selfless service to others, and it is central in Sikhism.
fact: Heroes, nurses and firefighters are often praised for selfless acts.
exercise: What does selfless mean? | *Thinking about other people's needs more than your own | Feeling very tired after a long day | Thinking only about what you want | Being the tallest in the class
exercise: «Seva means selfless service to others, and it is central in Sikhism.» Find and copy the word that shows seva is about helping others. | central | *service | Seva | Sikhism
exercise: «A free kitchen where anyone may sit on the floor and eat together, rich and poor side by side» suggests what about the people who run it? | *They put other people first | They are too busy to eat | They only think about themselves | They want payment from everyone
test: Which of these is a selfless act? | *A nurse stays late to care for a sick child and wants nothing back | Dan keeps all the sweets for himself | Sam hides his homework | Ella always wins every game
test: Mia gives her last biscuit to her little brother and wants nothing back. What does this show? | Angry: she is cross with him | *Selfless: she puts her brother first | Greedy: she wants more biscuits | Lazy: she does not want to cook
exam: The firefighter's ____ act saved the family from the flames. Which word fits best? | *selfless | sleepy | loud | careless
